{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HxQBk9MsDRDYsQrFTh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't promise \"the same cleaner every single time.\" Your setup is a regular cleaner plus a named backup, so the backup will sometimes come. Last year 7 of your 18 cleaners left, so cleaners will change again. The people you're emailing left partly because of that. If you promise \"every time\" and break it, you'll likely lose them for good. The email promises what you can actually keep.\n\n<final_document>\n**Subject:** We listened. Come back for $99.\n\nHi [First Name],\n\nWhen you left [Company], you told us why. The price was one reason. The other was seeing a different cleaner at your door too often. We heard you.\n\nHere's what's changed. Every customer now has one regular cleaner who gets to know your home. You also get a named backup, so if your cleaner is sick or on vacation, you'll know who's coming instead.\n\nAbout price: yes, the app services charge less. Here's what the difference pays for. Our cleaners are employees, not gig contractors. We pay them $21 an hour, and every visit is fully insured. If anything goes wrong, you deal with us directly.\n\nWe'd love to show you the difference. As a returning customer, your first cleaning is $99.\n\n[Book your cleaning] or just reply to this email.\n\nThanks,\n[Your Name]\nOwner, [Company]\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n- If you'd rather show the price gap in numbers, you could add \"about $25 less for a typical 3-bedroom.\" Being upfront about the cost tends to build trust with people who already know your prices.\n- If you have a stat on how long cleaners now stay, or how often the backup actually comes, it would back up the claim better than a promise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5376,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":